# ALLOWLIST. Everything is ignored unless named below.
#
# This is deliberately inverted. A denylist protects only the paths you thought of:
# the first version of this file ignored `spike/` and would have published the next
# practice project the moment it was called anything else, along with any brief or PRD
# dropped in the repo root.
#
# pica ships the METHOD - rules, commands, hooks, scripts. The projects it was derived
# from are evidence for the author, not content for anyone installing it, and they carry
# briefs, PRDs, real copy and client identifiers that are not redistributable. The
# findings those projects produced live in CHANGELOG.md, which is the durable form: a
# rule stated next to the failure that earned it, with no client data.
#
# To publish something new, add it here on purpose. If you find yourself adding a
# project directory, that is the signal to stop.

/*

# ---- the plugin surface: this is what pica IS ----
!/.claude-plugin/
!/commands/
!/hooks/
!/skills/

# ---- repo furniture ----
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE
!/.gitignore

# ---- docs: the design specs only, never the working brainstorm output ----
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/specs/

# ---- belt and braces ----
# These are ignored at ANY depth, including inside an allowlisted directory, so a
# captured artefact or a client brief cannot ride along inside skills/ or docs/.
.pica/
.audit/
.cmp/
node_modules/
*.docx
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.sketch
*.fig
